,"poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"adktyler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/886598","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/886598"}},{"id":"886605","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"889336","description":"","caption":"Cedar Rock Falls Lead In","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"adktyler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/886605","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/886605"}},{"id":"886599","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"889330","description":"Portage is on river right.","caption":"Cedar Rock Falls from Top River L","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"adktyler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/886599","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/886599"}},{"id":"886602","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"889333","description":"Portage is on river right.","caption":"Cedar Rock Falls from Middle River L","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"adktyler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/886602","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/886602"}},{"id":"886603","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"889334","description":"Portage is on river right.","caption":"Cedar Rock Falls from Bottom River L","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"adktyler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/886603","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/886603"}},{"id":"886604","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"889335","description":"Left line is more gnarly, right line is tight but pretty tame. The middle should be avoided due to logs in water.","caption":"Cedar Rock Falls Full L Line","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"adktyler","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/886604","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/886604"}}],"detail":{"id":"1429","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"This was first run in the late 1980s. The first big drop is called Cedar Rock Falls. The second big drop doesn't have a name. Here's the description from Don Morris, who ran it:\n\n\"I ran this section twice, shortly after Champion International started developing their easements. I think it was in the late 80s to mid 90s. The first time we thought Cedar Rock was Class 4; the second time we thought it was a 3 plus.\"\n\nHere's a video of the first drop: [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oDy93ROq1Ng](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oDy93ROq1Ng).\n\nThe section above Cedar Rock Falls by a half mile or so has some II+ stuff, too. Here's a video of that section: [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6eEga7olTr0](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6eEga7olTr0).\n\nFlow levels: You could paddle that section with a lot more water than 1,300, that's for sure. I'm not sure what the upper limit is, but at least 2,000 would be my guess.\n\nLastly, the put in on Quebec Brook is fine. Spring Cove is a weird place to end, though, since there's no takeout there. Once you pass that Blue Mountain Rd. bridge after the Cedar Rock Falls section, the next take it is the oxbow above the rapids before Spring Cove. Once you pass that, the next place to take out is the end of Santa Clara Flow. There are no rapids after Spring Cove that I recall.\n\n**Potsdam - Malone Area Reaches**\n\n[Chateaugay](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1284/) [Deer (Dickinson Center)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1289/)\n\n[Deer (Dickinson Center to Lawrenceville)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1290/) [Grass (1. Lampsons Falls to Downerville)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1310/)\n\n[Grass (Sec. 3)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1312/) [Grass (Sec. 4)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1311/)\n\n[Jordan](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1329/)[Little Trout](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1339/)\n\n[Marble](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1342/) [Meacham Lake Outlet](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4250/)\n\n[Raquette Sec. 3) Hannawa Falls](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/3747/)[Raquette 2) Piercefield to Parmenter Site](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1386/)\n\n[Raquette Sec. 4) Stone Valley](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1387/) [Salmon](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1406/)\n\n[Salmon (Chasm Falls)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4099/) [St. Regis](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1427/)\n\n[St. Regis, E. Branch](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1428/) [St. Regis, Middle Branch (Sec. 1)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1429/)\n\n[St. Regis, Middle Branch (Sec. 2)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1430/) [St. Regis, Middle Branch (Sec. 3)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1431/)\n\n[St. Regis, Middle Branch (Sec. 4.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1432/) [St. Regis, W. Branch (Sec. 1)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1435/)\n\n[St. Regis, W. Branch (Sec. 2)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1433/) [St. Regis, W. Branch (Sec. 3)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1434/)\n\n[Trout Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1446/)\n\n**[Google Map of New York Whitewater](https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=zjdnDE8H0TLg.kJnMWGapL4xk)**\n\n**[New York Whitewater Paddlers Facebook Group](https://www.facebook.com/groups/108070075877312/)**","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"9.5","correlations":[{"reachID":"1429","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"450","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"1300"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"WEST BRANCH ST. REGIS RIVER NEAR PARISHVILLE NY","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"04268800","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"362","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.99","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"44.59875","longitude":"-74.7372222"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/04268800","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/04268800/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"362","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["109251","114489"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-74.46178923811534,44.50584957223342],[-74.46181072819371,44.505895530917996],[-74.46270612819235,44.506420797583814],[-74.4626753281924,44.50717533091597],[-74.4628033281922,44.50726679758253],[-74.46312259485838,44.507152197582684],[-74.46360192819094,44.50715193091605],[-74.4638259281906,44.507311797582474],[-74.46379519485731,44.508